config VIDEO_NXS_CSI2
	tristate "Aliensense NXS camera map"
	depends on I2C && VIDEO_DEV
	select MEDIA_CONTROLLER
	select VIDEO_V4L2_SUBDEV_API
	select V4L2_FWNODE
	help
	  V4L2 sub-device driver for the camera map of an Aliensense NXS
	  device, the unit on a camera pod or a smart camera. The device runs
	  the image sensor. The driver builds one control per parameter row
	  the map serves, commits a frame's exposure, gain and frame period
	  as one write, and knows no sensor.

	  An NXS Hub's output takes a register-free routing node, which
	  reports each link's virtual channel to the receiver and starts the
	  link's camera door. The host tool programs the Hub itself.

	  To compile this driver as modules, choose M here: the modules will
	  be called nxs-csi2-core, the map client the driver shares with the
	  Jetson package, nxs-csi2, the sub-device, and nxs-hub-route, the
	  Hub output's routing node.
